SOURCE-AVAILABLE, NOT OPEN SOURCE
---------------------------------

This source code is published so that anyone can read it and verify what
Drippy actually does — what it measures, what it touches, and what leaves
your machine. A tool that asks you to trust its numbers should let you
check them.

Publication does not grant a licence. You may:

  - read, study and audit this source code
  - run the published builds for your own use
  - quote short excerpts when discussing or reporting on the project

You may not, without prior written permission from TRNSPNC Ltd:

  - copy, modify or redistribute this source code
  - use it, in whole or in part, in another product or service
  - offer it, or a derivative of it, as a hosted or commercial service

The impact factor tables (impact-factors.json, impact-sources.json) and the
methodology documents are published for scrutiny and citation. If you cite
them, cite the version.

A formal open-source licence may be applied to some or all of this project
in future. Until then, if you want to use any of it, please ask:
https://github.com/trnprnc/Drippy

NO WARRANTY: this software is provided "as is", without warranty of any
kind, express or implied. The environmental figures it reports are
estimates derived from published factors and carry a stated uncertainty
band; they are not a certified measurement and must not be presented as one.
